  "field": {
    "about": "Piece G3 of 0.32 (spec item 5609; rules 1.55 items 35 and 64): on the field after a won fight (the same fight, still running) an item's own action (combat/perk) is allowed or refused by its row here, `<item key>#<action id>`: \"allowed\", or the kind of refusal (`texts`: \"lasting\", it would give something lasting for AP alone, again and again; \"free\", it costs nothing the field counts). An action with no row is refused (`texts.unflagged`): a new action is flagged here when it is made (packages/engine/test/gaps-032.test.ts fails on one without a row). Seeded on 19 Nov 2026 from the old heuristic's answers (no action changed): the lead rules each \"free\" one.",
    "texts": {
      "lasting": "{label} waits for a fight: on the field it would give something lasting for AP alone, again and again.",
      "free": "{label} waits for a fight: on the field it would cost nothing the field counts.",
      "unflagged": "{label} waits for a fight."
    },
